  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Mozambique 2025 &#x2013; Team Lead</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In April 2024, the participatory design workshop &quot;ZamVis&#xe3;o&quot; was held in Quelimane, Mozambique, bringing together national and regional stakeholders under the guidance of the Dutch Disaster Risk Reduction &amp; Surge Support Team (DRRS Team). The workshop aimed to collaboratively develop a comprehensive vision to enhance flood and drought resilience, strengthen Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM), increase agricultural productivity, and promote economic development across the Zambezia Province.The Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands (EKN) in Mozambique is committed to supporting Mozambican authorities in mobilizing coordinated and effective follow-up actions based on the &#x201c;ZamVis&#xe3;o&#x201d; vision. The objective of this assignment is to support EKN in preparing for an upcoming donor conference, with a specific focus on the technical content.</narrative>
  </description>
